\
Elvis might have dated countless girls, but it was at least partially because his manager wanted him to. Colonel Tom Parker was tireless in marketing Elvis as the ultimate lady's man, and the idea that Elvis might finally find "the one" was a nightmarish thought, indeed. Parker's control over Elvis' love life was never more evident than in 1956 when Elvis's girlfriend, June Juanico, told reporters she was his steady. Immediately, Parker sought to squash the news, having Elvis "confess" to a different reporter, "I got about 25 girls I date regular. She's just one of the girls."\'a0\

